    "title": "How to live stream Dodgers vs Diamondbacks: MLB Opening Weekend, TV channel",
    "text": "The Los Angeles Dodgers continue their Opening Weekend series against the Arizona Diamondbacks on Friday after a dominant statement to begin their title defense. MORE: MLB preseason power rankings Advertisement Mar 26, 2026; Los Angeles, California, USA; Arizona Diamondbacks outfielder Corbin Carroll (7) hits a single to right field against Los Angeles Dodgers starting pitcher Yoshinobu Yamamoto (not pictured) during the fourth inning at Dodger Stadium. Mandatory Credit: Kirby Lee-Imagn Images How To Watch Dodgers vs Diamondbacks Date: Friday, February 27, 2026 Time: 10:10 p.m. ET TV Channel: SportsNet LA, MLB Network, MLB.TV Live Stream: Fubo (try for free) The Dodgers enter this matchup with serious momentum following an 8–2 Opening Day win, powered by a five-run middle inning and contributions throughout a loaded lineup. Andy Pages delivered the key blow with a go-ahead three-run homer, while Yoshinobu Yamamoto set the tone on the mound with six strong innings, allowing just two runs and striking out six. With stars like Shohei Ohtani, Mookie Betts, and Freddie Freeman surrounding emerging contributors, Los Angeles once again looks like one of the most complete teams in baseball as they chase a third straight World Series title. Live Stream Dodgers vs Diamondbacks Advertisement For Arizona, the opener showed both promise and concern. Zac Gallen was sharp early with four scoreless innings before unraveling in the fifth, as the Diamondbacks struggled to contain Los Angeles’ relentless offense. Offensively, Arizona managed just two runs and couldn’t sustain pressure after an early spark, highlighting the need for more consistent production from a lineup built around Ketel Marte and Corbin Carroll. If the Diamondbacks can stabilize their pitching and generate more timely hitting, they have the talent to respond, but the Dodgers clearly hold the early edge in this series. Live stream Dodgers vs Diamondbacks with Fubo: Start your free trial now! Advertisement With Fubo, you can watch live television without cable on your phone, TV, or tablet. Fubo is the streaming leader in baseball and offers the most MLB you can get without cable, including local sports packages, MLB Network, MLB.TV and top national channels like ABC, FOX, CBS, ESPN, FS1, MTV, Comedy Central, and many more. They carry everything from MLB to NBA, NFL, NHL, NCAA, and the best part is you can try it out today for free. Regional restrictions may apply. If you purchase a product or register for an account through one of the links on our site, we may receive compensation. — Enjoy free coverage of the top news & trending stories on The Big Lead — MARCH MADNESS: 2026 Sweet 16 TV schedule, game times & dates for NCAA Tournament NFL: Jaxon Smith-Njigba, Seahawks make NFL history with blockbuster deal NBA: Warriors’ Moses Moody suffers serious knee injury on dunk attempt SPORTS MEDIA: Select CBS, TNT Sports record highest-rated opening day in NCAA Tournament history ENTERTAINMENT: WWE’s Liv Morgan chugs beer to fire up Boston crowd ahead of ‘Monday Night RAW’ VIRAL: Aryna Sabalenka devours $100 Miami Open ‘Golden Glizzy’ after QF berth",
